PROMPT:
Use case: character turnaround for image-to-3D (Tripo multi-view input), NON-HUMANOID creature (four-legged animal).
REFERENCE IMAGES (attached in this order): (1) the concept sheet of the creature (a lineup with an H silhouette, a 3/4 view and four model views): identity reference for the DESIGN only (body build, head and face, fur or skin, colours, parts worn or attached, markings, proportions). Keep the same design. Do NOT copy the lineup layout, the H silhouette, the dashed guide lines, any text, or the pose of the 3/4 view or of the model views. (2) the placement template: a flat grey canvas with two slightly lighter rectangles; it is NOT artwork: use only its canvas shape and size, the two placement rectangles and their common floor line. 
STYLE CORE (ASHLAR art direction, mandatory): moderately stylized hand-painted dark fantasy in the spirit of Diablo Immortal (the Diablo III / Diablo Immortal family look). NOT photoreal, NOT Diablo IV realism, NOT cartoon, chibi, anime, cel-shaded or toy-like. Proportions follow real anatomy; exaggeration goes only to the identity features (heroes: hands, feet and class props slightly oversized; monsters: their signature features pushed further). Strong readable silhouette, clear value grouping, clean colour blocking: a dominant colour, a secondary colour and a small accent, plus neutrals. Surfaces are SIMPLE: broad painted planes with soft gradients and a few crisp highlights; detail comes from big shapes (large torn edges, plates, straps, bones, cracks, patches), never from texture. No micro texture: no pores, fabric weave, leather grain, scratches, stains, speckle noise, fine grunge or photoreal PBR. Low detail never means flat: keep clear 3D form shading with a lit side, a shadow side, big soft fold shadows and darker occlusion in deep folds. No black cartoon outlines.
T-POSE RULES: keep the concept's design, build and smooth painted low-detail surface; only the pose changes. Keep the concept's hand-painted form shading: every big fold and cloth layer has a lit plane and a large dark shadow plane (deep shadow in fold recesses, under capes, hoods, collars, belts and sashes, inside splits); roughly a third of each cloth surface in shadow; never one evenly lit flat colour. One neutral white light from above and slightly from the camera side, the SAME in every view; no side light, no rim light, no coloured light, no glow or bloom. Cloth is one plain clean shape (no ragged fringe, no loose strips). Hands empty; hand-held weapons and props are built separately. Perfectly flat neutral mid-grey background; no text, no human silhouette.
CONTENT: no crosses, no real saints, prayers or religious symbols; ASHLAR's church sign is the Wedge (a keystone shape), only where the brief asks for it. No gore emphasis and no blood splatter (Act III blood accents are small painted stains only); heroes show no wounds and no blood. Adults only; no nudity, no anatomical detail, no sexualised poses; no likeness of any real person. Never stage hanged bodies.
B01 Sexton's Dog, variant A: an old, sad, grave-risen mastiff, a very large heavy dog of Saint-Bernard build (about 0.72 H tall including the shoulder fur and 1.4 H long including the tail, H = adult human height). Massive broad head with a deep wrinkled brow, loose hanging jowls drawn as one broad plane, long soft brown ears hanging flat against the sides of the head, a short pale cream blaze down the forehead and a pale cream muzzle with a dark nose, small tired dark eyes. Very wide deep chest and heavy forequarters; thick shaggy dark-brown fur (#4A3526) built from a few big chunky tufts with clean painted edges (a ruff around the neck and chest, feathering behind the front elbows, the tail), never individual hairs. A wide flat iron-grey collar (#5A5F66) with a few rivets circles the neck; from its front centre a short chain with one large round dull-brass ring (#B59A5B), the lantern-hook, hangs on the chest down to elbow height, drawn as one chunky ring hugging the chest. Two or three large smooth pale tan-grey patches of grave soil on the rump and hind flanks. Large paws with pale toes and short dark claws. A long shaggy tail hanging down and back as one thick tapered shape. Smooth painted low-detail surface; no exposed bone, no wounds, no gore, no glow. Prologue creature: no accent colour; the brass ring is the only bright touch.
Canvas and placement: ONE landscape image with exactly the shape of the template (3:1), with TWO full-body views of the same creature side by side: left = the FRONT view (the creature seen from the front, facing the camera), right = the BACK view (the true back, not a mirrored front). Each view is painted inside its lighter rectangle of the template: the paws rest on the bottom edge of the rectangle, the highest point of the creature touches the top edge, and the creature is centred horizontally in it. Both views share one floor line and one scale; whole body visible, nothing cropped, no overlap. Do NOT draw the rectangles, no outline, no floor line, no cast shadow: the background is perfectly flat neutral mid-grey (#808080) everywhere, with only a faint soft contact shadow directly under the paws.
POSE = NEUTRAL STANDING (the most important requirement). This creature is a four-legged animal: there is NO T-pose and nothing is held out. It stands square, calm and symmetric on all four legs, like the rest pose of a skeleton rig. Proportions as in the concept: a large heavy dog: head about one third of the body length and very broad, thick short neck, deep chest, strong straight forelegs, hind legs with their natural relaxed standing angle, big paws; body (nose to rump) about 1.7 times the height at the shoulders; the tail hangs down to about hock height.
- LEGS: all four paws flat on one ground line; the two front legs vertical and parallel under the shoulders with a clear gap of empty background between them; the two hind legs in the same relaxed standing posture, also parallel with a clear gap between them; the stance about as wide as the chest. Paws point straight forward: never splayed outward, never braced forward, never crouched, never lunging, no leg lifted, no leg crossed.
- BODY: spine straight and level, no sway and no hunch, no tilt; the left and right halves are mirror images in stance. The belly is clearly above the ground; only the four paws touch it.
- HEAD: carried in the concept's natural carriage (forward and heavy, not raised and not lowered further), pointing straight at the camera in the FRONT view and straight away from it in the BACK view; never turned, tilted, sniffing or snarling; mouth closed; ears hanging in their resting position.
- TAIL: hangs down and slightly back as one simple tapered shape, so that it is seen in the BACK view; never curled, never raised, never tucked between the legs.
- Thin or loose parts (hair tufts, whiskers, chain links, the tail tip) become chunky simple shapes that hug the body; nothing hangs free in a thin line.
- The FRONT and BACK views have the same height, the same body width and the same floor line. In the FRONT view the head is not enlarged by perspective; in the BACK view the rump is not enlarged.
Camera: eye level, orthographic look, no perspective, no tilt, no 3/4 angle, no view from above.
Fidelity: keep the concept's body build, face, fur and surface exactly (a heavy animal stays heavy; NO added muscle definition, NO exposed ribs or bone, NO claws or teeth beyond the concept, NO extra anatomy or ornaments the concept does not show). Only the pose changes.
Left out of the pose: nothing (no weapon). The collar and the ring stay as body parts.
Asymmetric details stay on the same body side in every view: The animal is bilaterally symmetric. Keep these placements the same in every view: the pale cream blaze is centred on the forehead and the muzzle; the brass ring hangs at the centre of the chest (seen in FRONT, hanging in front of the chest in LEFT and RIGHT, hidden in BACK); the pale grave-soil patches sit on the upper rump and hind flanks on BOTH sides (one large patch on the upper rump in each side view, patches across both hips and the base of the tail in BACK); the collar rivets run evenly around the neck.
No text, labels, numbers, logo, watermark or scenery. No human silhouette.

